00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:11.810
FRANCISCO URIBE: The mission
of the computer vision platform

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:15.880
is to enable our partners to
implement the next generation

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.140
enterprise AI solutions.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:23.000
And this focus on the enterprise
has led in the last few years

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.550
to significant breakthroughs
of application of AI

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.740
across multiple verticals.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.420
Industries are
using our technology

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.610
to detect damage
in their facilities

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.030
for predictive maintenance.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.940
Media and
entertainment companies

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.760
are using our technology to
implement intelligent content

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.140
management systems.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.160
And the focus of this talk,
health care organizations

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:44.810
and labs are using
our technology

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.560
to analyze medical imagery
to optimize radiology

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.000
and pathology workflows.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.650
So a few examples of this.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.700
The brain team has been
using computer vision

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:01.710
to detect diabetic retinopathy
leveraging fundus images

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.230
or images from the
back of the eye.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.470
Now this is critical work, and
a significant breakthrough,

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:10.560
because diabetic retinopathy is
one of the leading and fastest

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.890
growing causes for blindness.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.860
If this disease is not
being detected on time,

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.140
it can lead to
irreversible blindness.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.000
Now the bad news
is that there's not

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.010
that many physicians
in the world that can

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:24.700
detect this disease on time.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:27.540
So it's very critical for
us to empower these doctors

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:33.150
with AI technology so that
we can prevent blindness.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.840
And this is especially true
in underserved populations

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:41.570
where there's not enough
coverage of doctors.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:43.640
Another example is the
work from our brain team

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:46.670
who has been using computer
vision algorithms on top

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:51.140
of tissues lights to detect
different forms of cancer.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.730
This is also very critical
work because detecting cancer

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:59.210
in these sort of slides can take
multiple hours from physicians

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:02.010
and requires multiple
years of training.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:09.449
And to explain why, one single
slide is immensely large

00:02:09.449 --> 00:02:14.290
and has over one
gigapixel of resolution.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:19.790
It is also very critical for
us to help those doctors detect

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:23.130
and analyze these images to
improve different patient

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:23.630
outcomes.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:29.360
Now these two use causes can be
implemented with our computer

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.530
vision tuning today, which,
to recap, is comprised

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:36.965
of two sets of products,
our pre-trained products

00:02:36.965 --> 00:02:40.180
or the Vision API and
our customizable products

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:43.030
called AutoML Vision.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.360
Our pre-trained products
require no training.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.360
They're completely plug
and play through a code.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.730
You can just simply
issue a REST call

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:52.320
to be able to get
predictions from your data.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:55.250
These are great for generic
and well understood use cases.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.830
And our AutoML
Vision products can

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.732
be customized for
your own data, uses

00:02:59.732 --> 00:03:01.190
behind the scenes
[INAUDIBLE] state

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.860
of the art neuro-architecture
search and hyperparameter

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:09.480
tuning technology, and is great
for more specialized use cases.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.820
Now last year we
introduced AutoML Vision

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.853
for image classification.

00:03:13.853 --> 00:03:16.020
And we're very humbled by
the popularity and success

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:16.770
of this tool.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:20.130
But we know that this is only
part of the toolkit required

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.320
to do computer vision,
especially as we tackle

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.780
more complex health scenarios.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:30.080
So for that reason, I'm
very excited to announce

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.090
AutoML Vision object detection.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:37.310
This product allows you to
detect not only the presence,

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:39.460
but the location,
body box coordinates

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:42.330
of objects in your images.

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:46.400
And this whole experience
is very seamless.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.120
And it has the
same model quality

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.970
as the rest of the
AutoML product family.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:56.330
And to explain how to use this
technology in a real use case,

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.240
I'm inviting Ben Litchfield,
software development manager

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:01.268
from IDEXX, onstage.

00:04:01.268 --> 00:04:02.693
Come on.

00:04:02.693 --> 00:04:03.610
BEN LITCHFIELD: Great.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:04.110
